"Design decisions (2026-08-08, user-approved): (1) reference detection is TYPE-BASED and specific to entity ids -- fields declared with the macro's EntityId type are the reference fields; other-field parameterization deferred. (2) Ordering: do build-entity-blobs-from-component-blobs-id-less-blob-types FIRST. With distinct per-component blob types, value selection embeds directly INTO the blob type (EntityId-typed blob fields become a reference-selector enum) instead of a parallel modifier struct; true component row types unaffected. (3) Instantiation then takes a context parameter to resolve selectors (external named/long-lived entities vs intra-batch handles). (4) No new macro state needed: the component+field list for the selector enum derives from already-parsed component declarations at enum-generation time. (5) Future: imprinting an entity blob onto an EXISTING entity covers per-component prefab instantiation; entity-level instantiation = imprint onto a fresh entity."